dataModelChanges.details:
A new module-scope mutable binding, let deliveryBoardOpen: (() => void) | undefined;, declared before the panelHost construction (extension.ts:398) so it is in scope for the onOpenDeliveryBoard closure assigned there. At extension.ts:897, the call is rewritten as `const deliveryBoard = registerDeliveryBoard({ ... });` (identical arguments, identical closing `});` line) with a new statement on the next line, `deliveryBoardOpen = deliveryBoard.open;` — the call itself is never chained (never `registerDeliveryBoard({...}).open`), so its own `registerDeliveryBoard({` ... `
  });` textual shape is preserved byte-for-byte. This is required: board-icon.test.ts:42 regex-matches /registerDeliveryBoard\(\{([\s\S]*?)
  \}\);/ against extension.ts's raw source, and board-wiring.test.ts:75-77,144-145 does EXT.indexOf('registerDeliveryBoard({') then slices to EXT.indexOf('
  });', call) — both break if the call's closing line becomes anything other than `  });`. The closure captures deliveryBoardOpen by reference, so reading it after assignment resolves correctly even though the closure was created ~500 lines earlier.
